From: AEMONET-Dev <267029939+AEMONET-Dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:20:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] shader: insert group barriers for split one-wave wave64 LDS
 groups (port VIctory-macOS#148)

When VICTORY_WAVE64_HALVES=1 is enabled, 33-64 thread one-wave wave64
compute groups that use LDS (e.g. step-distance ray-march prep) are split
across two 32-lane waves on Apple Silicon. Insert thread-group barriers
before LDS reads/atomics fed by prior LDS writes and drop WaveSize(64)
when synced so D3DMetal runs them cleanly.

Verified on M5 Max with FSR 3.1.6 (VICTORY_FIDELITYFX_DIR=C:\victory\ffx-pc):
GPU time dropped to 158-282 ms/frame, 0 XPC errors, 0 fragment mismatches,
0 shader refusals, 5 total [ERROR] (34816 B mesh only).
